Comments:
1. Evaluator: Kiana Setoodehnia, December 11, 2024.
2. The energies and spin-parities are from M. S. Basunia et al., Nucl. Data Sheets 197, 1 (2024). The 5168-keV state was removed. The 5218.8- and 5226-keV states are 
   combined into one state at 5219.6 keV based on measurements by G. T. Koldste et al., Phys. Rev. C 87, 055808 (2013) and Ibid 89, 064315 (2014); G. Lotay et al., 86,
   042801 (2012); S. Almaraz-Calderon et al., 86, 065805 (2012); and K. Setoodehnia et al., 87, 065801 (2013).
3. The spectroscopic factors are from P. M. Endt At. Data Nucl. Data Tables 19, 23 (1977).
4. The gamma-ray partial widths for resonances come from those of the mirror states scaled for the 30S resonance energies. The mirror partial widths are from M. S. 
   Basunia et al., Nucl. Data Sheets 197, 1 (2024).
5. The proton partial widths are calculated from spectroscopic factors provided by P. M. Endt At. Data Nucl. Data Tables 19, 23 (1977). The upper limits are based 
   on spectroscopic factors of C^2S < 0.01.
6. The experimental rate is matched to the TALYS statistical model rate above T = 1.5 GK.
